  "# Cisco IOS to Juniper Junos Migration Plan for R1 and R2\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nThis document outlines the migration of Cisco IOS routers **R1** (AS 65000) and **R2** (AS 65001) to Juniper Junos equivalents. Configurations were extracted from the latest snapshot `snap_20260227_162240_42686b` in the parsed_outputs table. Key features translated: interfaces, OSPF (Area 0 with redistribution), BGP (iBGP internal, eBGP peering with policy controls), prefix-lists/route-maps to policy-options, management ACLs to firewall filters.\n\nDevices:\n- **R1**: border router, mgmt 192.168.100.101, Lo0 1.1.1.1\n- **R2**: border router, mgmt 192.168.100.102, Lo0 2.2.2.2\n\nAssumptions:\n- Interface mapping: GiX → ge-0/0/X.0, LoopbackX → lo0.unitX\n- No crypto/certificates, licenses, or non-essential features migrated\n- Tested in lab before production\n- Hardware replacement or reimaging assumed\n\n## Current Cisco IOS Configurations Summary\n\n### R1 (AS 65000)\n- **Interfaces**:\n  - Lo0: 1.1.1.1/32 (OSPF A0)\n  - Lo11: 11.11.11.11/32\n  - Gi1: 10.1.12.1/24 to R2 (OSPF A0)\n  - Gi2: 10.1.13.1/24 to R3 (OSPF A0)\n  - Gi4: 192.168.100.101/24 mgmt\n- **OSPF 1**: RID 1.1.1.1, redistribute BGP 65000\n- **BGP 65000**: RID 1.1.1.1\n  - iBGP: 3.3.3.3 (AS65000, Lo0 src)\n  - eBGP: 10.1.12.2 (AS65001), import bgp_in (permit net20), export bgp_out (permit net10)\n  - Network: 1.1.1.1/32, redistribute OSPF\n- **Policies**:\n  - Prefix net10: 192.168.10.0/24\n  - Prefix net20: 192.168.20.0/24\n  - VTY ACL: permit 192.168.100.0/24\n\n### R2 (AS 65001)\n- **Interfaces**:\n  - Lo0: 2.2.2.2/32 (OSPF A0)\n  - Lo22: 22.22.22.22/32\n  - Gi1: 10.1.12.2/24 to R1 (OSPF A0)\n  - Gi2: 10.1.24.2/24 to R4 (OSPF A0)\n  - Gi4: 192.168.100.102/24 mgmt\n- **OSPF 1**: RID 2.2.2.2, redistribute BGP 65001\n- **BGP 65001**: RID 2.2.2.2\n  - iBGP: 4.4.4.4 (AS65001, Lo0 src)\n  - eBGP: 10.1.12.1 (AS65000), import bgp_in (permit net10), export bgp_out (permit net20)\n  - Network: 2.2.2.2/32, redistribute OSPF\n- **Policies**: Same prefix-lists, VTY ACL same\n\n## Translated Juniper Junos Configurations\n\n### R1\n\n\tsystem {\n\t    host-name R1;\n\t    domain-name local;\n\t    login {\n\t        user cisco {\n\t            class super-user;\n\t            authentication {\n\t                plain-text-password \"cisco\";\n\t            }\n\t        }\n\t    }\n\t    services {\n\t        ssh;\n\t        web-management {\n\t            http {\n\t                interface ge-0/0/3.0;\n\t            }\n\t            https {\n\t                system-generated-certificate;\n\t                interface ge-0/0/3.0;\n\t            }\n\t        }\n\t    }\n\t    syslog {\n\t        host 192.168.100.10 {\n\t            any any;\n\t        }\n\t    }\n\t}\n\tinterfaces {\n\t    lo0 {\n\t        unit 0 {\n\t            family inet {\n\t                address 1.1.1.1/32;\n\t            }\n\t        }\n\t        unit 11 {\n\t            family inet {\n\t                address 11.11.11.11/32;\n\t            }\n\t        }\n\t    }\n\t    ge-0/0/0 {\n\t        unit 0 {\n\t            description \"to_R2_Gi1\";\n\t            family inet {\n\t                address 10.1.12.1/24;\n\t            }\n\t        }\n\t    }\n\t    ge-0/0/1 {\n\t        unit 0 {\n\t            description \"to_R3_e0/0\";\n\t            family inet {\n\t                address 10.1.13.1/24;\n\t            }\n\t        }\n\t    }\n\t    ge-0/0/2 {\n\t        disable;\n\t    }\n\t    ge-0/0/3 {\n\t        unit 0 {\n\t            description \"to_Mgmt_e1\";\n\t            family inet {\n\t                address 192.168.100.101/24;\n\t                filter {\n\t                    input mgmt-filter;\n\t                }\n\t            }\n\t        }\n\t    }\n\t}\n\tfirewall {\n\t    family inet {\n\t        filter mgmt-filter {\n\t            term permit-mgmt {\n\t                from {\n\t                    source-address {\n\t                        192.168.100.0/24;\n\t                    }\n\t                }\n\t                then accept;\n\t            }\n\t            term deny-all {\n\t                then {\n\t                    discard;\n\t                }\n\t            }\n\t        }\n\t    }\n\t}\n\tpolicy-options {\n\t    prefix-list net10 192.168.10.0/24;\n\t    prefix-list net20 192.168.20.0/24;\n\t    prefix-list local-lo 1.1.1.1/32;\n\t    policy-statement bgp_in {\n\t        term permit-net20 {\n\t            from {\n\t                prefix-list net20;\n\t            }\n\t            then accept;\n\t        }\n\t        term deny-rest {\n\t            then reject;\n\t        }\n\t    }\n\t    policy-statement bgp_out {\n\t        term permit-net10 {\n\t            from {\n\t                prefix-list net10;\n\t            }\n\t            then accept;\n\t        }\n\t        term deny-rest {\n\t            then reject;\n\t        }\n\t    }\n\t    policy-statement advertise-to-bgp {\n\t        term local-lo {\n\t            from {\n\t                prefix-list local-lo;\n\t            }\n\t            then accept;\n\t        }\n\t        term ospf-routes {\n\t            from protocol ospf;\n\t            then accept;\n\t        }\n\t        term reject-rest {\n\t            then reject;\n\t        }\n\t    }\n\t    policy-statement bgp-into-ospf {\n\t        term accept-bgp {\n\t            from protocol bgp;\n\t            then accept;\n\t        }\n\t    }\n\t}\n\trouting-options {\n\t    router-id 1.1.1.1;\n\t}\n\tprotocols {\n\t    ospf {\n\t        router-id 1.1.1.1;\n\t        export bgp-into-ospf;\n\t        area 0.0.0.0 {\n\t            interface lo0.0 {\n\t                passive;\n\t            }\n\t            interface ge-0/0/0.0;\n\t            interface ge-0/0/1.0;\n\t        }\n\t    }\n\t    bgp {\n\t        group iBGP {\n\t            type internal;\n\t            local-address 1.1.1.1;\n\t            family inet {\n\t                unicast {\n\t                    export advertise-to-bgp;\n\t                }\n\t            }\n\t            neighbor 3.3.3.3 {\n\t                peer-as 65000;\n\t            }\n\t        }\n\t        group eBGP {\n\t            type external;\n\t            neighbor 10.1.12.2 {\n\t                peer-as 65001;\n\t            }\n\t            family inet {\n\t                unicast {\n\t                    import bgp_in;\n\t                    export bgp_out;\n\t                }\n\t            }\n\t        }\n\t    }\n\t}\n\n### R2\n\n\tsystem {\n\t    host-name R2;\n\t    domain-name local;\n\t    login {\n\t        user cisco {\n\t            class super-user;\n\t            authentication {\n\t                plain-text-password \"cisco\";\n\t            }\n\t        }\n\t    }\n\t    services {\n\t        ssh;\n\t    }\n\t    syslog {\n\t        host 192.168.100.10 {\n\t            any any;\n\t        }\n\t    }\n\t}\n\tinterfaces {\n\t    lo0 {\n\t        unit 0 {\n\t            family inet {\n\t                address 2.2.2.2/32;\n\t            }\n\t        }\n\t        unit 22 {\n\t            family inet {\n\t                address 22.22.22.22/32;\n\t            }\n\t        }\n\t    }\n\t    ge-0/0/0 {\n\t        unit 0 {\n\t            description \"to_R1_Gi1\";\n\t            family inet {\n\t                address 10.1.12.2/24;\n\t            }\n\t        }\n\t    }\n\t    ge-0/0/1 {\n\t        unit 0 {\n\t            description \"to_R4_e0/0\";\n\t            family inet {\n\t                address 10.1.24.2/24;\n\t            }\n\t        }\n\t    }\n\t    ge-0/0/2 {\n\t        disable;\n\t    }\n\t    ge-0/0/3 {\n\t        unit 0 {\n\t            description \"to_Mgmt_e1\";\n\t            family inet {\n\t                address 192.168.100.102/24;\n\t                filter {\n\t                    input mgmt-filter;\n\t                }\n\t            }\n\t        }\n\t    }\n\t}\n\tfirewall {\n\t    family inet {\n\t        filter mgmt-filter {\n\t            term permit-mgmt {\n\t                from {\n\t                    source-address {\n\t                        192.168.100.0/24;\n\t                    }\n\t                }\n\t                then accept;\n\t            }\n\t            term deny-all {\n\t                then {\n\t                    discard;\n\t                }\n\t            }\n\t        }\n\t    }\n\t}\n\tpolicy-options {\n\t    prefix-list net10 192.168.10.0/24;\n\t    prefix-list net20 192.168.20.0/24;\n\t    prefix-list local-lo 2.2.2.2/32;\n\t    policy-statement bgp_in {\n\t        term permit-net10 {\n\t            from {\n\t                prefix-list net10;\n\t            }\n\t            then accept;\n\t        }\n\t        term deny-rest {\n\t            then reject;\n\t        }\n\t    }\n\t    policy-statement bgp_out {\n\t        term permit-net20 {\n\t            from {\n\t                prefix-list net20;\n\t            }\n\t            then accept;\n\t        }\n\t        term deny-rest {\n\t            then reject;\n\t        }\n\t    }\n\t    policy-statement advertise-to-bgp {\n\t        term local-lo {\n\t            from {\n\t                prefix-list local-lo;\n\t            }\n\t            then accept;\n\t        }\n\t        term ospf-routes {\n\t            from protocol ospf;\n\t            then accept;\n\t        }\n\t        term reject-rest {\n\t            then reject;\n\t        }\n\t    }\n\t    policy-statement bgp-into-ospf {\n\t        term accept-bgp {\n\t            from protocol bgp;\n\t            then accept;\n\t        }\n\t    }\n\t}\n\trouting-options {\n\t    router-id 2.2.2.2;\n\t}\n\tprotocols {\n\t    ospf {\n\t        router-id 2.2.2.2;\n\t        export bgp-into-ospf;\n\t        area 0.0.0.0 {\n\t            interface lo0.0 {\n\t                passive;\n\t            }\n\t            interface ge-0/0/0.0;\n\t            interface ge-0/0/1.0;\n\t        }\n\t    }\n\t    bgp {\n\t        group iBGP {\n\t            type internal;\n\t            local-address 2.2.2.2;\n\t            family inet {\n\t                unicast {\n\t                    export advertise-to-bgp;\n\t                }\n\t            }\n\t            neighbor 4.4.4.4 {\n\t                peer-as 65001;\n\t            }\n\t        }\n\t        group eBGP {\n\t            type external;\n\t            neighbor 10.1.12.1 {\n\t                peer-as 65000;\n\t            }\n\t            family inet {\n\t                unicast {\n\t                    import bgp_in;\n\t                    export bgp_out;\n\t                }\n\t            }\n\t        }\n\t    }\n\t}\n\n## Migration Phases\n\n### 1. Preparation\n- **Backup**: Snapshot current Cisco configs (already done: snap_20260227_162240_42686b).\n- **Procure Hardware**: Juniper devices with equivalent interfaces (e.g., EX/QFX series).\n- **Lab Validation**: Load Junos configs in lab, verify OSPF/BGP peering with emulated peers (R3/R4), policies, reachability.\n- **Update Inventory**: Add new Junos devices to Nornir/DB.\n- **Schedule Window**: Off-peak maintenance, notify stakeholders.\n- **Pre-stage Configs**: Save Junos set commands as load files.\n\n### 2. Execution (Per Device, Sequential: R1 then R2 to minimize outage)\n- **R1**:\n  1. Shut peers (OSPF/BGP graceful shutdown if supported).\n  2. Replace/reimage to Junos, set mgmt IP.\n  3. Load/apply config: `load set /path/to/r1.conf`, `commit check`, `commit`.\n- **R2**: Same, after R1 stable (eBGP peer).\n- Coordinate cabling: Ensure physical links match.\n\n### 3. Verification\n- **Interfaces**: `show interfaces terse` up/up.\n- **OSPF**: `show ospf neighbor`, `show ospf database`.\n- **BGP**: `show bgp summary`, `show route advertising-protocol bgp <peer>` matches policies.\n- **Routes/Ping**: Verify net10/net20 propagation, end-to-end pings (use probe subagent).\n- **Logs/Syslog**: Check for errors.\n- **Take Snapshot**: `take_snapshot` post-migration.\n\n### 4. Rollback\n- Spare Cisco hardware ready.\n- If issue: Power off Junos, reconnect Cisco, restore config from backup.\n- Graceful: Pre-announce routes via communities to divert traffic.\n\n## Risks & Mitigations\n| Risk | Mitigation |\n|------|------------|\n| Peering Failure | Lab test, rollback plan |\n| Policy Mismatch | Diff configs pre/post |\n| Hardware Diff | Exact interface mapping |\n| Outage >5min | Sequential migration |\n\n**Report Generated**: 2026-02-27 from DB snapshot snap_20260227_162240_42686b\n\n---\n*OLAV Ops Orchestrator*": "filename",
